      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "The electronic configurations of the transition elements usually follow the Aufbau principle, with two exceptions: chromium and copper. Chromium is [Ar] 3d5 4s1 and copper [Ar] 3d10 4s1, because a half-filled (3d5) or completely filled (3d10) d subshell is especially stable; it makes the electron cloud more symmetrical."
          },
