          {
            "type": "callout",
            "tone": "tip",
            "title": "Which electrons go first?",
            "text": "When a transition metal forms an ion, the 4s electrons are lost before the 3d electrons. So Fe ([Ar] 3d6 4s2) becomes Fe2+ [Ar] 3d6 and then Fe3+ [Ar] 3d5."
          },
